WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.394
There is no single best local language model for every user.

00:00:04.394 --> 00:00:09.468
A useful choice depends on the task, hardware, memory, speed, context, output quality,

00:00:09.468 --> 00:00:13.372
concurrency, privacy, and operational tolerance for slow or unstable behavior.

00:00:13.372 --> 00:00:16.104
Local inference is a hardware-constrained engineering decision.

00:00:16.104 --> 00:00:19.617
The complete configuration includes model architecture, parameter count, quantization,

00:00:19.617 --> 00:00:23.521
context size, runtime, acceleration backend, offload, prompt template, generation settings,

00:00:23.521 --> 00:00:24.301
and cooling.

00:00:24.301 --> 00:00:30.547
A model that leads one public benchmark may perform poorly on a specific machine or task.

00:00:30.547 --> 00:00:34.450
Benchmarks use particular prompts, scoring methods, hardware, software, and settings.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:39.134
They are useful for forming a shortlist, not declaring a permanent winner.

00:00:39.134 --> 00:00:42.648
Quality has several dimensions: factuality, instruction following, coding ability,

00:00:42.648 --> 00:00:46.551
writing style, domain performance, refusal behavior, hallucination risk, and consistency.

00:00:46.551 --> 00:00:52.016
A larger score or parameter count does not guarantee the behavior an application needs.

00:00:52.016 --> 00:00:53.968
Performance also has multiple dimensions.

00:00:53.968 --> 00:00:57.090
Time to first token matters in interactive use.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.042
Generation speed affects reading pace.

00:00:59.042 --> 00:01:01.384
Prompt processing matters for long documents.

00:01:01.384 --> 00:01:05.288
Throughput and stability matter for batch jobs and multiple users.

00:01:05.288 --> 00:01:09.972
The best choice is the smallest or simplest configuration that meets the

00:01:09.972 --> 00:01:12.704
real requirement with acceptable quality and margin.

00:01:12.704 --> 00:01:16.217
Start with the task and machine, test representative work,

00:01:16.217 --> 00:01:19.340
and scale only when measured shortcomings justify it.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:24.024
Include total operating cost in the decision: hardware purchase, electricity, cooling, storage,

00:01:24.024 --> 00:01:26.757
engineering time, maintenance, downtime, and review effort.

00:01:26.757 --> 00:01:30.660
A free model can still be expensive to operate badly.
